\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Israel shekel fixed 1.2 pct higher on dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1998\par 12:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The battered Israeli shekel was fixed stronger against the dollar at 4.2600 shekels in nervous trade on Friday, against 4.3110 on Thursday, recouping about 1.2 percent after sharp recent losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It is very nervous trade at the moment. The market is bouncing around. It is small amounts that are moving the market because it is so nervous," a dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. \par \par \uc2  Friday marked the first day of gains after four consecutive sessions of drops. The shekel slumped badly over the last week shedding more than 10 percent amid uncertainty in global markets. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the fix on Thursday, the dollar sailed through what dealers had termed a resistance level of 4.3 and quickly reached above 4.4 shekels, triggering expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank Hapoalim dealer said he saw no sign of the current trend letting up. \par \par \uc2  "It is unclear what will happen. Nervous trading is likely to continue for days. The world markets are impacting what is going on here but to a large extent we have our own mini crisis," he said. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 4.2600 shekels, against 4.3110 on Thursday. The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 4.7008 shekels against 4.7918 shekels on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 3.6025 shekels per 100 yen compared with 3.7116 on Thursday, and against the mark at 2.6124 shekels compared with 2.6999 shekels on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the early afternoon after the fix, the shekel was trading at 4.1698 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua901lmi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
