\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel rallies against dollar in afternoon. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jennifer Freidlin \par \uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Profit-taking by foreigners helped strengthen the battered Israeli shekel against the dollar in late afternoon trading on Thursday following publication of the representative rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 1415 the shekel was trading at 4.2397 against the dollar compared with Thursday's fix of 4.3110. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel has rebounded on a bit of profit-taking by foreigners," a dealer at Bank Leumi said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "There was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whatsoever," a Bank Leumi dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Thursday marked the fourth straight session of big losses for the shekel during which it shed more than 10 percent versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the fix on Thursday, the dollar sailed through what dealers had termed a resistance level of 4.3 and quickly reached above 4.4 shekels, triggering expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the shekel had come under pressure mostly from foreign banks, with some selling by Israeli borrowers seeking to repay foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked loans. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing foreigners selling because they are selling around the world. Because of that the Israeli private sector is getting cold feet and repaying \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans early," said Jonathan Katz, chief economist at Solid Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the shekel selling did not reflect a crisis of confidence in the economy but that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 4.3 to signal the market that it would not tolerate a further sharp depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 4.7918 shekels against 4.5084 shekels on Wednesday. In late afternoon, the baset was 4.6882. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the mark at 2.6999 shekels compared with 2.5263 shekels on Wednesday, and shed more than 12 percent against the yen to a fix of 3.7116 to 100 yen versus Wednesday's 3.2614. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua801jgh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
