\par\par \b \uc2  Wrap: Israel  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Awaits Central Bk Move On Shekel \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 16:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--If the shekel continues its dramatic plunge against the dollar - nearly 10% in just three days - the Bank of Israel should start selling dollars on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to check its fall, analysts said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Although they differed over the timing of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - whether it would begin Friday or the beginning of next week - analysts agreed that a free-fall for the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be disastrous despite the country's oft-cited strong economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the shekel lost 5.3% of its value against the dollar, plunging to a new low of ILS4.3110 from the previous day's fixing at ILS4.0960. Just one week ago, a dollar quote at ILS4.000 would have been inconceivable; yet astounded dealers saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall as far as ILS4.4700 to the dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained silent. Trading room managers reported no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Jacob Frenkel, in an interview with Israel radio from the U.S., projected calm. \par \par \uc2  "One thing is clear - there is much more volatility in the financial markets," he said. "The phenomenon is a worldwide occurrence in which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... are undergoing significant changes. And the shekel, which is also connected to the same system, is evidencing volatility," Frenkel said during his visit to Washington for the International Monetary Fund meeting. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to defending the upper and lower limit of the shekel's trading band - one that allows a fluctuation of 15% on either side of a gradually depreciating midpoint. In the first half of 1997, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $7 billion to tame an overly strong shekel. \par \par \uc2  Yet some analysts criticized the bank's "hands-off" approach to the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, stressing that if Frenkel waits until the shekel nears its lower limit, it may be too late to catch up with the inflationary spiral already evident in local shops and businesses. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1441GMT \par \par \uc2  1199 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua8004s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
