\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Propper -2: Frenkel Responsible For Shekel Stability \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 12:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The head of the Manufacturer's Association of Israel called Thursday on Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel to return from the U.S. and help calm the country's battered foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel is attending meetings of the International Monetary Fund in Washington, as is Finance Minister Yaakov Neeman. \par \par \uc2  In an interview on Israeli radio, Dan Propper said the shekel's (ILS) depreciation of nearly 9.0% since the start of October wasn't yet an outright collapse, but must be monitored carfeully. \par \par \uc2  "I think the (Bank of Israel) governor must be here now ... because he is responsible for the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Propper said. \par \par \uc2  In Frenkel and Neeman's absence this week, the shekel fell below the ILS4.000 level compared with the dollar for the first time ever. At 0932 GMT, the shekel was trading at around ILS4.2400 to the dollar, a decline of 3.5% compared with Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing at ILS4.0960. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts attributed the fall to global economic troubles that have led to the outflow of foreign capital and to hedging by Israeli companies especially vulnerable to exchange-rate fluctuations because of their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans. \par \par \uc2  "What is happening today is effect of the great (economic) turmoil around the world," Propper said. \par \par \uc2  Propper said a depreciation as far as 10% was a welcome correction to the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value against the dollar, since the shekel's relative strength in the last two years has restricted the economy's ability to grow. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, Propper said, "if there is a steep slide (in the shekel) and a collapse begins, then of course I think the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and do everything to save this capital market. All of us need a stable basis to advance the economy." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1000GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua8005u0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
