\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 's Frenkel:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  No Way To Run A Market \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 18:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel on Thursday aimed to allay fears over the shekel's 5.3% slide against the dollar, stressing that regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the wasn't the right way to oversee the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel is of course obligated to defend the limits of the trading band," Frenkel told Israel radio from Washington, where he is attending a meeting of the International Monetary Fund. "We worked hard to develop an effective ... foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. To \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily isn't the right way." \par \par \uc2  Frenkel didn't say whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the tide of dollar purchases driving down the shekel had been ruled out as a stopgap measure. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate 15% on either side of a gradually depreciating midpoint. The shekel's dive to ILS4.3110 to the dollar Thursday, the third sharp drop in as many days, placed it within 11% of its lower limit, compared to its 20% distance at the start of the week. \par \par \uc2  "It isn't a question of worrying (over the depreciation), but of understanding the material," Frenkel said. "The panic reflects a misunderstanding of what is happening." \par \par \uc2  Frenkel said heightened foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk was something market players had to take into account, and attributed the decline in large part to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan-taking by the Israeli business sector. \par \par \uc2  "The foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market isn't a place for amateurs. Whoever enters this market knows there is a chance to gain and a chance to lose," Frenkel said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts, however, expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the shekel continues its dramatic fall. In addition, they forecast a rise in the 9.5% discount rate is in store for November to curb the inflationary pressure of the shekel's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Israeli legislators and economic leaders criticized Frenkel, along with Finance Minister Yaakov Neeman, for remaining in the U.S. during a sensitive time for local capital markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief defended his sojourn, saying: "The mission we set for ourselves was to present the Israeli economy before (foreign economic and investment officials) and to stress that it's a place worth entering." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1608GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua8004wu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
