\par\par \b \uc2  Wrap:  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Forex \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Or Rate Hike Urged \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 17:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "I think they should have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  already at the ILS4.000 (level)," said Giora Zarechansky, an analyst at the Ilanot Batucha Investment House Ltd. "They might have stopped (the depreciation) at that level." \par \par \uc2  Victor Shohet, chief economist at Ofek Securities and Investments Ltd., urged the other alternative at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's disposal: "It's definitely time to put up interest rates. I think it's one step too late and I wouldn't be surprised if they announce an interest rate hike even today." \par \par \uc2  Shohet estimated an increase of two to three percentage points to the 9.5% discount rate would be the minimum required to affect the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to announce the November rate on October 26. \par \par \uc2  Whether the bank brings up interest rates or starts selling some of its $21.7 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to dampen the depreciation, analysts said that Israel should forget earlier expectations of 4.0-5.0% inflation for 1998, and begin revising the 1999 outlook as well. \par \par \uc2  Zarechansky estimated consumer prices will rise 3.0% in October alone, based on current shekel-dollar rates. And if that trend continues into November, 1998 inflation may well be closer to 7.5% to 8.0%, he said. \par \par \uc2  As for the effects on other economic indicators, analysts said it's too early to tell. \par \par \uc2  "I still think our fundamentals are very strong so we are nowhere near the situation of countries like South Korea or Russia," Shohet said. "I don't look at what is happening and say we are headed for catastrophe." \par \par \uc2  "Some companies will be hurt and their ability to function normally will be somewhat lessened. It's difficult to gauge at the moment. But we will see some bankruptcies - it will be on the margins, for companies who have taken too much risk," he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1504GMT \par \par \uc2  1199 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua8004t3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
