\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Shohat -2: Govt Should Revise '99 Inflation Forecast \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 14:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Opposition Labor party legislator Avraham Shohat called for calm after the shekel (ILS) fell 5.3% Thursday against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Shohat urged economic policymakers to take measures to calm the country's capital markets. \par \par \uc2  "I say we're at a critical point," said Shohat, a former Finance Minister under the previous Labor government, in an Israel radio interview. \par \par \uc2  "I hope we're at the end of the depreciation, because the Israeli economy, with all of its strengths...isn't an island of stability." \par \par \uc2  International financial crises have touched off outflows of foreign capital from the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Israeli companies and banks seeking to hedge against the exchange rate risk of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans also boosted demand for the dollar to unprecedented highs. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at ILS4.3110 to the dollar Thursday, compared to the ILS4.0960 fixing on Wednesday. The Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 11.3% against the dollar since the start of October. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade or raise interest rates, both options cited by analysts as a way to soothe market fears. \par \par \uc2  "If there's a depreciation of 15% or more within a few weeks then it's clear that inflation will spiral," Shohat said. "The question is when will this stop, and here I call on the Israeli public not to panic." \par \par \uc2  At the same time, he said, "there is a large danger to the stability of the Israeli economy if the depreciation reaches more than 20% or 25%." \par \par \uc2  Shohat said the government should revise already its forecast of 4.0% inflation for 1999 due to the shekel's fall. Inflation in 1998 was expected to reach 4.0% to 5.0% in 1998 before the sharp depreciation occurred, but now analysts say that figure will likely jump at least 2 percentage points. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Finance Minister Yaakov Neeman and Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel remained in Washington for a meeting of the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Shohat joined other Israeli economic officials in urging the two policymakers to return. "When the economy is in such a sensitive situation...they should take the first plane and head home," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Neeman is scheduled to return to Israel Friday, the Finance Ministry\par said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spokesman wasn't immediately available to confirm\par Frenkel's date of return.\par    -By Michele Gershberg; 9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1218GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua8004ky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
