\par\par \b \uc2  Merrill Lynch/ \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  -2: Drastic Drop May Spur  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1998\par 15:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The shekel's (ILS) depreciation in recent days doesn't signal a protracted period of turmoil for the Israeli economy, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should stabilize after a period of weakness, Merrill Lynch said Wednesday in a report. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, Merrill Lynch expects to see the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady the shekel" in the case of an overly speedy decline, the report said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel fell below the ILS4.000 level to the dollar for the first time ever Tuesday to ILS4.0110. and declined another 2.1% Wednesday to ILS4.0960. The sharp depreciation triggered expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market or an increase to the 9.5% discount rate by November. \par \par \uc2  The flight of some foreign capital from the market, as well as the efforts of some customers to hedge their exposure to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans were likely behind the shekel's decline this week, the Merrill Lynch report said, echoing the estimates of local foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, we feel that fundamentals do not support a period of protracted turbulence," the report said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1343GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua7002yc\pa