\par\par \b \uc2  Wrap/ \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Also Seen As An Option \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 1998\par 18:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "My rough guess is that we'll see interest rates rise within the next week," Shohet said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement isn't scheduled to announce the discount rate for November until the end of October. Shohet said only a steep increase of two or three percentage points would effectively influence the market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel's other option to curb the depreciation would be to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade by selling dollars, an alternative "that's not inconceivable," Shohet said. \par \par \uc2  In the first half of 1997, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in trade and bought $7 billion to tame an overly strong shekel. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts, however, said that the recovery of European bourses and the dollar's weakness on world markets during Tuesday gave grounds to believe the Israeli foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would calm in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's drop was better viewed as a delayed reaction to turmoil on international markets while Israeli exchanges were closed for a long holiday weekend, they said. Low liquidity also worked against the shekel and deepened the impact of moderate-sized transactions. \par \par \uc2  In addition, most of the trade was between banks, as many individual customers head for vacation during the abbreviated work week of the Succoth holiday. Their absence exacerbated the rise because "usually when you hit psychological (low shekel) levels, customers will sell (dollars)," and soften the declines spurred by interbank trading, said Chaim Fromowitz, head of trading at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Fromowitz said reasons for deep panic were absent from trading Tuesday, with little evidence of foreign banks or brokerages buying dollars or of exporters seeking to close foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans en masse. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Israel wouldn't comment on the shekel's sharp decline or\par possible policy changes.\par -By Michele Gershberg;9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-10-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1601GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1196 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua6001ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
