\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt -2: Neeman Also Says Govt Will Stay Out \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1998\par 13:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Tuesday "there's no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which has been roiled in recent days by the volatility on global markets. \par \par \uc2  Netanyahu said he spoke with Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel Tuesday and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief holds the same view. \par \par \uc2  The prime minister spoke at a news conference he called to address economic issues. \par \par \uc2  At the same news conference Finance Minister Yaakov Neeman also said the government and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  don't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The shekel (ILS) has been swinging up and down against the dollar since Friday, when it dropped 2.7% in illiquid trading to ILS3.8750 to the dollar at the Bank of Israel fixing. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the shekel regained 1.9% against the dollar amid profit-taking, and was fixed at ILS3.8010. But it slipped as low as ILS3.8800 Tuesday morning because of the sharp drop on Wall Street before rebounding to ILS3.8400 at 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 01-09-98 \par \par \uc2  1111GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9107hej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
