\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Israel shekel fixed 2.7 pct down on dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By David Rosenberg \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 13:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Aug 28 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed on Friday 2.7 percent weaker against the dollar at 3.8750 in a day of panicked trading spurred by volatile world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign banks joined the shekel selling late in the session, adding to the pressure on the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  "All the (world) markets are collapsing, and people are panicking. There is a strong need to diversify portfolios, which until now have been mainly in shekels. People are now balancing their portfolios," said Yaacov Harpaz, dealing room manager at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel began depreciating in early August from a level of about 3.65 on the dollar after the Bank of Israel made a surprise 1.5 percentage point cut in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The pace of depreciation gained momentum on Thursday. In the last two days, the shekel's total loss against the dollar has reached 3.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at American-Israel Bank said world stock markets, especially those in East Asia, had given investors in Israel the jitters. "You had some nice falls in the Far East, and in the U.S. you'll see the same thing later in the day," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said borrowers with dollar-linked loans were seeking to repay in expectation of further dollar-shekel volatility. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Yaacov Neeman sought to calm the market by stressing that the market was free to determine the appropriate shekel rate. \par \par \uc2  "In the State of Israel the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is determined by supply and demand. This is the only way to calm investors," Neeman told Israel Army Radio. \par \par \uc2  The shekel easily breached what some dealers had said would be an initial resistance point at about 3.87 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The American-Israel dealer said 3.91-3.92 would constitute the next barrier and that it was a strong one. Harpaz said the shekel could weaken further before it meets serious resistance. \par \par \uc2  "The first resistance point should be 3.90, but it won't be a strong one. We're heading to four-double-O," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Harpaz said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the shekel breached 4.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.8750 shekels, against 3.7730 on Thursday. The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 4.1354 shekels against 4.0142 shekels on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 2.7071 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.6422 shekels on Wednesday, and against the mark at 2.1686 shekels compared with 2.0872 shekels on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the early afternoon, the shekel was trading at 3.8732 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8s01rh8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
