\par\par \b \uc2  Israel shekel tumbles vs dollar in panic trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1998\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Aug 28 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel weakened sharply against the dollar in Friday morning trading in what dealers described as a panic atmosphere. \par \par \uc2  At 0740 GMT, the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 3.8377 to the dollar, a loss of about 1.7 percent from the Thursday representative rate of 3.7730. \par \par \uc2  "All the (world) markets are collapsing, and people are panicking. There is a strong need to diversify portfolios, which until now have been mainly in shekels. People are now balancing their portfolios," said Yaacov Harpaz, a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  Friday's losses continued from a sharp one percent weakening of the shekel on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Yaacov Neeman sought to calm the market by stressing that the market was free to determine the appropriate shekel rate. \par \par \uc2  "In the State of Israel the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is determined by supply and demand. This is the only way to calm investors," Neeman told Israel Army Radio. \par \par \uc2  Pnina Lipman, a trader at American-Israel Bank, said there was heavy interbank trading as well as trading by private investors and companies. She said much of the demand was coming from investors bailing out of the stock market and companies seeking to repay dollar-and dollar-linked loans. \par \par \uc2  "In my opinion, (the shekel) will go to 3.90 next week. I think 3.87 is the next barrier, then 3.90," Lipman told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Harpaz said he thought the shekel would push past 3.90 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think in the next few days we'll be trading outside 3.90 shekels. The shekel is overvalued and a devaluation of between 10 and 15 percent is very good for the economy," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Harpaz said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the shekel breached 4.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, the shekel was trading at 4.0782 against Thursday's 4.0142 representative rate. \par \par \uc2   for Bank of Israel rates. ((David Rosenberg, Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8s01r8d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
