\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel weakens against basket, dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 15:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The shekel weakened against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in active trading on Tuesday, leaving the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further from the edge of its trading band than on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "There were lots of customers in the market because (exchange rates) are still low. Now is a great opportunity to cover (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) exposure," said a dealer at Israel Continental Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel representative rate was fixed 0.33 percent away from the strong limit of its trading band against the basket. That compared with 0.14 percent at Monday's fix, which had prompted concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, although it could be expected to if the basket rate approaches the limit. \par \par \uc2  The trading band straddles 15 percent each side of a crawling midpoint. The shekel has been close to the strong edge for some time, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the shekel had strengthened recently as companies sold dollars to cover end-of-the-month payments but that pressure on the dollar had now eased. \par \par \uc2  The dollar comprises 50 percent of the basket. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.6500 shekels, against 3.6450 on Monday. The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.8899 shekels against 3.8809 shekels on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 2.5221 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.5039 shekels on Monday, and against the mark at 2.0469 shekels compared with 2.0415 shekels on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon, the shekel was trading at 3.6504 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Jennifer Friedlin, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8400y58\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
