\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - Shekel nears strong end of trading band. \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In TEL AVIV story headlined "Israeli shekel nears strong end \par \par \uc2   of trading band", please read in fifth graph"...has not \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January..."instead of"...has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2   since April..."correcting month. \par \par \uc2  A corrected version follows. \par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The shekel strengthened against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed in on the strong limit of its trading band against the basket. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel said the shekel closed just 0.14 percent away from the edge of the band. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at United Mizrahi Bank said it was possible the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the coming days. \par \par \uc2  "If the dollar-mark rate rises and the shekel-dollar rate remains the same, then the shekel could fall out the strong edge of its band and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. \par \par \uc2  The trading band straddles 15 percent each side of a crawling midpoint. The shekel has been close to the strong edge for some time, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at First International Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was likely that the shekel would continue strengthening. "We can't see anything that will make the dollar or basket rise," he said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel also advanced against the dollar on Monday as banks sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy into a big dollar-linked bond issue by the Treasury, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading started with a dollar supply, part of it due to the government issue of dollar-linked bonds today," said the First International dealer. \par \par \uc2  The government issued 300 million shekels worth of dollar-linked Gilboa bonds on Monday and is due to issue another 350 million shekels on August 17. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.6450 shekels, against 3.6500 on Friday. The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.8809 shekels against 3.8918 shekels on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 2.5039 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.5305 shekels on Friday, and against the mark at 2.0415 shekels compared with 2.0479 shekels on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon, the shekel was trading at 3.6450 to the dollar. ((Shoshanna Solomon, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) REUTERS. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du8300vz1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
