\par\par \b \uc2  Israel shekel stable against dlr ahead of CPI. \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1998\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, July 13 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel closed stable against the dollar and weakened slightly against the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in quiet trading on Monday ahead of the consumer price index (CPI), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market opened at the same levels it closed at on Friday, which caused the basket to strengthen slightly due to dollar weakness in the world," a dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. "It then remained static at that level." \par \par \uc2  The dealer said that despite the shekel's strength, which was expected to trigger shekel selling, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  players were waiting for the Central Bureau of Statistics to announce the June CPI on Wednesday (1400 GMT). \par \par \uc2  "The shekel is 0.9 percent away from the strong edge of the trading band, (but) trading is slow and it seems that people are waiting for the CPI," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer added he expected the June index to ease 0.1 percent, which could lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates, weakening the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trades within a band whose midpoint is 15 percent above and below the band's edges. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the shekel hit the edge of the band. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.6660 shekels against 3.6680 shekels on Friday. The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.8971 shekels against 3.8915 shekels on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 2.5829 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.5917 shekels on Friday, and against the mark at 2.0247 shekels compared with 2.0088 shekels on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the shekel was trading at 3.6665 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Jennifer Friedlin, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211, x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7d00uqp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
