\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Frenkel -2: Details Of Liberalization Not Final \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1998\par 13:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Authorities haven't yet said exactly what liberalization measures will be enacted around May 1, and that void has made the market and public even more jittery - a mood the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor sought to allay. \par \par \uc2  'Changes in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are something characteristic of all \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets,' Frenkel said. 'I wouldn't turn all these things into drama. We're talking about a long-term program of liberalization, of improving the way the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market functions, of creating conditions where markets set the prices and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the authorities don't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't involved in the market at present, he added. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel also reaffirmed, as he has done repeatedly in recent weeks, that he expected the shekel to be declared fully convertible on schedule, adding that details of the planned foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalization measures would be announced 'very soon.' \par \par \uc2  The proposals have been forwarded to the Finance Ministry, where they are being reviewed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1129GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4702xxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
