\par\par \b \uc2  Israel CPI, dollar bonds finish up on dlr gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, April 5 (Reuters) - Israeli inflation-linked and dollar-linked bonds ended sharply higher on Sunday, after the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated by 1.3 percent against the dollar last week, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * Government bonds general: +0.49 pct to 111.96 \par \par \uc2  * CPI-linked government bonds: +0.49 pct to 108.88 \par \par \uc2  * Unlinked government bonds: +0.11 pct to 120.70 \par \par \uc2  * Dollar-linked government bonds: +1.48 pct to 120.37 \par \par \uc2  * Bank of Israel short-term Makam bills: +0.07 pct to 118.06 \par \par \uc2  Volume including Makams was a heavy 258 million shekels. \par \par \uc2  "People expect the shekel to continue depreciating and that pushed the dollar and CPI-linked bonds up," said Roy Meir of Simodan Investments. \par \par \uc2  The Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated .50 percent against the dollar on Friday on fears the government's planned \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms would lead to a weakening of the shekel. \par \par \uc2  A weaker shekel would result in inflation, thus causing the increase in the indexed bond market. \par \par \uc2  The government said it would implement a host of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms on or around April 30, in coordination with Israel's 50th anniversary. \par \par \uc2  But Tiki Hadad of the IBI Investment House said the simultaneous rises in the dollar, CPI-linked and unlinked bonds indicated a split market opinion on what would happen next. \par \par \uc2  "It's very rare that these three rise together. It shows that some people aren't convinced the dollar will continue to rise," she said. \par \par \uc2  Hadad said she did not expect the dollar-linked bonds would continue rising because she thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a continued shekel depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has high reserves and it is watching over inflation very closely," she said. \par \par \uc2  Yields on long-term indexed bonds fell to 4.80 percent and 5.15 percent on the medium-term bonds and held steady at 6.0 percent on the short bonds, Hadad said. \par \par \uc2  Unlinked bonds also rose, albeit relatively modestly, Meir said, with yields holding steady at 11.1 percent on the long Shahar bond and to 12.80 percent on the long Gilon bond. \par \par \uc2  Yields on the Gilboa dollar-linked bond held steady at 5.5 percent, Hadad said. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate was fixed at 3.6350 against the dollar on Friday compared with 3.6170 shekels on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Note: Makams are zero-coupon unlinked certificates with durations of three months to one year. The Bank of Israel issues Makams to absorb liquidity. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.64 shekels) ((Jennifer Friedlin, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x233, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du450839z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
