\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel weakens ahead of CPI figure. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, March 11 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel on Wednesday weakened against the dollar and the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  before Sunday's announcement of February's consumer price index (CPI), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A stronger dollar overseas helped to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the shekel. \par \par \uc2  "It was pretty quiet. The shekel is still very close to the (edge of the) band, only 0.2 percent away," a dealer at Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel, pegged to the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, has been trading very close to the limit of the band on its strong side. Traders believe the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon to prevent the shekel from appreciating beyond its band. \par \par \uc2  "The inflation figures could lend some buoyancy...to the dollar rate, if the CPI figure comes in around zero percent as expected," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A low CPI figure could spur the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower interest rates, which have supported a strong shekel. \par \par \uc2  Due to the Jewish holiday of Purim, the Bank of Israel will not set representative rates on Thursday or Friday. The next representative rate will be set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5890 against 3.5860 shekels on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.8219 shekels against 3.8208 shekels on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7794 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.8088 shekels on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9575 shekels compared with 1.9589 shekels on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the shekel was trading at 3.5906 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2   for Bank of Israel rates. ((Tova Cohen, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du3b00ba1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
