\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli Shekel Up Vs Dlr Late; Probing Trading Band Ceiling \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 14:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The shekel (ILS) strengthened against the dollar late Monday afternoon, hitting the strongest point in its trading band and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was within a hair's breadth away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers at Bank Hapoalim and Israel Discount Bank said the shekel struck its ceiling close to the 1330 GMT fixing. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reported the shekel at 0.1% from its ceiling at the fixing, but dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely for the following day. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the shekel at ILS3.5850 to the dollar, a rise of 0.1% compared with Friday's fixing at ILS3.5870. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of ILS3.5820 to ILS3.5920 to the dollar during the session. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at ILS3.5830. \par \par \uc2  Trading was generally quiet and volumes were moderate, dealers said. The shekel opened weaker against the dollar due to the dollar's rise on foreign markets. \par \par \uc2  But routine corporate sector dollar sales strengthened the shekel during the day, a dealer at First International Bank of Israel said. \par \par \uc2  'There wasn't a panic,' she said, 'but technically there were a lot of loans for conversion.' \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said the current market trend is to strengthen the shekel, due to the attraction of taking out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans and benefiting from high Israeli interest rates when they convert the money into shekels. \par \par \uc2  When the shekel hits the strongest point in its trading band, the Bank of Israel has been committed to buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early January, when it briefly bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over a period of two weeks. In the first half of 1997, however, the Bank of Israel bought $7 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and defend the trading band. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-03-98 \par \par \uc2  1357GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du390226r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
