\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli inflation-indexed bonds end down. \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Israeli inflation-linked bonds continued to drop on Wednesday, and traders were split over the possibility that prices would recover in the near term. \par \par \uc2  * Government bonds general: -0.20 pct to 110.91 \par \par \uc2  * CPI-linked government bonds: -0.28 pct to 108.44 \par \par \uc2  * Unlinked government bonds: +0.03 pct to 118.06 \par \par \uc2  * Dollar-linked government bonds: +0.02 pct to 117.37 \par \par \uc2  * Bank of Israel short-term Makam bills: +0.02 pct to 115.74 \par \par \uc2  Volume including Makams was a moderate 132 million shekels. \par \par \uc2  "The market is continuing to fall, but we are heading towards the end of the drop," said Roy Meir of Simodan Investments. "Yields won't go beyond five percent." \par \par \uc2  Meir recalled that in July 1996 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when yields on inflation-indexed long bonds hit 5.1 percent. Therefore, he predicted, buying support would likely develop before yields reached that level in anticipation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acting again. \par \par \uc2  Yields on inflation-linked long bonds rose to 4.9 percent on Wednesday, Meir said. Yields on indexed short bonds rose to 5.5 percent and to 4.7-4.8 percent on medium bonds. \par \par \uc2  But Yair Elek of Israel Discount Bank predicted tough times ahead for the indexed market because the Bank of Israel would maintain its strict monetary stance, therefore high real interest rates, even if the outlook is for low inflation this year. \par \par \uc2  "Inflation was seven percent last year, so there's no way the Bank of Israel is going to settle for anything higher," he said. \par \par \uc2  Unlinked bonds continued higher on Wednesday with yields falling to 12.4 percent, Meir said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-linked bonds were also up as the shekel weakened against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation was circulating in the market, Elek said. Yields on the dollar-linked bonds dropped to 5.6 percent, he said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the U.S. representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.6040, strengthening from 3.6010 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Note: Makams are zero-coupon unlinked certificates with durations of three months to one year. The Bank of Israel issues Makams to absorb liquidity. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.60 shekels) ((Jennifer Friedlin, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2b059qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
