\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Israel Spent 3B ILS In '97 To Defend Trading Band \b0\par\par\uc2 154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1998\par 11:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Israel estimates it spent 3 billion shekels in 1997 to sterilize the more than $7 billion it bought to defend the shekel trading band, Finance Ministry accountant-general Shy Talmon said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Talmon reported the figure to the Knesset Finance Committee on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In 1996, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some 2 billion shekels to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The band was widened June 18, 1997, to put a halt to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near-daily purchase of dollars. \par \par \uc2  The wider band prevented Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade for six months, but in late December and early January the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in trade after the shekel reached the strongest point in its trading band. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1049GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1t00s2u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
