\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel Down Vs Dollar: No  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1998\par 14:52\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Israeli shekel traded lower compared with the dollar late on Monday, weakened by the dollar's strength against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.5610 to the dollar, a weakening of 0.2% compared with Friday's close of 3.5540 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.5590 to 3.5660 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at 3.5620. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes were low, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the shekel was weakened by the dollar's rise against the Deutsche mark. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading Monday to defend the shekel's trading band, although dealers expected it would be forced to re-enter the market again in the near future. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the shekel was just grazing the strongest point in its declared trading band. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed on Dec. 29 after a six-month hiatus, spurred by the resumption of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan-taking. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading almost daily, buying hundreds of millions of dollars to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Customers take advantage of Israel's high discount rate - now at 13.4% - by borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , converting it into shekels and benefiting from the rate differential. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1352GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du1c000me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
