\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Loan-Taking Slower Last Half '97 \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1998\par 14:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowed dramatically in the last half of 1997, to an average of $170 million per month from $710 million per month in the first half of the year, the Bank of Israel reported Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel attributed the change to customers' perception that the risk of taking credit in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had increased. \par \par \uc2  In the first half of 1997, customers took advantage of the differential between Israel's high discount rate and that of other countries by borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and converting it into shekels. \par \par \uc2  The high rate of conversions strengthened the shekel beyond the strongest point in its trading band. This forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $7 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first half of the year to defend the trading band. \par \par \uc2  Borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowed after the Bank of Israel widened the shekel's trading band and cut the discount rate to 12.7% from 13.9% on June 18, reducing the rate differential. The trading band was slowly widened to allow a 15% fluctuation from a gradually depreciating midpoint, as opposed to the earlier 7% range. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hoped the wider band would put an end to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading. But in September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the discount rate to 13.4%, making loan-taking attractive to customers again. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed Dec. 29, after a six-month hiatus, and has continued on an almost daily basis since then. Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers expected to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading again Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1302GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1c0096r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
