\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel loses vs dollar in quiet trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed lower against the dollar in quiet trading on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "During early trading, the shekel weakened following the rise of the dollar abroad. But when the dollar started declining, the shekel recovered slightly, only to start falling again towards the end of the trading day," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  She said the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded 0.1-percent above the lower limit of its band, the shekel's strong side, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most trading sessions since December 31 to prevent the shekel from exceeding the band. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5610 shekels against 3.5540 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7910 against 3.7898 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.6945 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.7159 on Friday and against the mark at 1.9615 shekels compared with 1.9690 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5620 shekels. \par \par \uc2  ((Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1c09b6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal276