\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel Buys Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Via Foreign Bank \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 14:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Israel has begun buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via a a foreign investment house, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  This marks the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ever bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a foreign investment house as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading. \par \par \uc2  'The reason is to introduce competition,' the source said. 'If we use more than one source, there is competition over the price.' In the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly through a so-called global box - a voice hookup between the trading rooms of all the Israeli banks. \par \par \uc2  One foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer differed on the competition claim, saying the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading only when the shekel has reached the strongest point in its trading band and that 'it's no secret the Bank of Israel wants to turn the shekel into a convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' Using a foreign broker now increases exposure to foreign markets in advance of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalization measures planned for May, he explained. \par \par \uc2  The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan to make the shekel a fully convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May. \par \par \uc2  This week, the Bank of Israel had bought as of Wednesday more than $200 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, the source said. \par \par \uc2  -By Michele Gershberg; 9722-537-6985; mgershberg@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1323GMT \par \par \uc2  (corrected 9:12 am est) \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du18005tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
