\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Dollar Sales Dominate Market \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 14:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading Thursday for the sixth time in the last seven trading sessions, following a six-month hiatus, to weaken the shekel and defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said that the dollar's rise in world markets this week made it the more attractive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell. The shekel thus strengthened to the strongest point within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounted to some $20 million at 1245 GMT, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Israel's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is primarily affected by interest-rate decisions, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements abroad and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalization. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates over the past three years designed to tame inflation have artificially strengthened the shekel. This has encouraged customers to borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and convert the money into shekels to take advantage of the differential between Israel's discount rate and lower rates abroad. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more than $7 billion in the first half of 1997 to weaken the shekel and keep it within its band, the band was widened on June 18 to allow a fluctuation of 15% from a gradually depreciating midpoint, as opposed to the earlier 7%. The discount rate was lowered to 12.7% from 13.9% that same day. \par \par \uc2  The widening of the trading band and the lowering of the discount rate increased the perceived risk of borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The initial concern subsided, however, and the discount rate was\par raised to 13.4% last September and has stayed there since. Due to these\par developments, foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loans have surged, putting the shekel\par back at the strongest point within its band.\par -By Michele Gershberg; 972-2-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1311GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du18005t8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
