\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Dollar Sales Dominate Market \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 14:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading Wednesday for the fifth time in the last six trading sessions, following a six-month hiatus, to weaken the shekel and defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise in world markets this week made it the more attractive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. The shekel thus strengthened to the strongest point within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading last Tuesday. The exchange was closed Thursday for New Year's Day and as usual on Saturday and Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Israel's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is primarily affected by interest-rate decisions, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements abroad and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalization. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates over the past three years, designed to tame inflation, have artificially strengthened the shekel. This has encouraged customers to borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and convert the money into shekels to take advantage of the differential between Israel's discount rate and lower rates abroad. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more than $7 billion in the first half of 1997 to weaken the shekel and keep it within its band, the band was widened June 18 to allow a fluctuation of 15% from a gradually depreciating midpoint, as opposed to the earlier 7%. The discount rate was lowered to 12.7% from 13.9% that same day. \par \par \uc2  The widening of the trading band and the lowering of the discount rate increased the perceived risk of borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1336GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du17004ey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
