\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Bank of Israel buys $100 mln in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying $100 million to prevent the shekel from appreciating beyond its trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Towards the end of the trading day the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market buying about $100 million," said a dealer at the First International Bank of Israel. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is pegged to a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The basket rate hovered at the lower limit, the shekel's strong side, of the trading band throughout Wednesday, due to the weakness of the mark and yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began buying dollars in the local market towards the end of last week, marking its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last June, when foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform and a sharp interest rate cut temporarily weakened the shekel. Since then the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gradually strengthened. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was quiet today and the shekel continued to weaken against the dollar after the dollar rose abroad," the dealer said, adding that the shekel recovered some of its losses by midday when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened slightly abroad. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5640 shekels against 3.5630 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7898 against 3.7892 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.6913 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.6659 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9506 shekels compared with 1.9521 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5590 shekels. \par \par \uc2  ((Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du17017jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
