\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Move Not Triggered By Politics \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 14:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $120 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading for the fourth time since Dec. 29 to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading wasn't affected by Foreign Minister David Levy's resignation, which has destabilized Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales continued Tuesday, strengthening the shekel to the strongest point in its trading band and forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is primarily affected by interest rate decisions, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements abroad and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalization, and less so by political events, even if they appear to threaten the government's survival. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading last Tuesday for the first time in six months, and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in three trading days since. The exchange was closed Thursday for New Year's Day and as usual on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates over the past three years, designed to tame inflation, have artificially strengthened the shekel. That's encouraged customers to borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and convert the money into shekels to take advantage of the differential between Israel's discount rate and lower rates abroad. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1311GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du160032c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
