\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  Shekel Lower Vs Dollar:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par 14:56\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Israeli shekel traded lower compared with the dollar late Tuesday due to the dollar's strength on international markets. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth time in trading since Dec. 29, buying about $120 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel and defend its trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.5630 to the dollar, a weakening of 0.3% against Monday's close of 3.5520 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.5550 to 3.5650 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at 3.5620. \par \par \uc2  Ilan Zadka, a senior trader at United Mizrahi Bank, said that sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for shekels continued Tuesday, keeping the shekel strong compared with the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that determines its position within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose against the shekel, however, due to its rise on world markets, Zadka said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading volumes were moderate, dealers said.\par -By Michele Gershberg;9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  06-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1356GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du16000cu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
