\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars to prevent the shekel from appreciating beyond its trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market, buying $100-$150 million," a dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is pegged to a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The basket's rate hovered at the lower limit -- the shekel's strong side -- of the trading band on Tuesday, boosted by the weakness of the mark and yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the local market twice last week, marking the first \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last June, when foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform and a sharp interest rate cut temporarily weakened the shekel. Since then the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gradually strengthened. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's representative rate on Tuesday was fixed lower against the dollar, after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against the mark and yen overseas. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5630 shekels against 3.5520 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7892 against 3.7881 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.6659 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.6682 on Monday, and against the mark at 1.9521 shekels compared with 1.9602 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5600 shekels. \par \par \uc2  ((Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du16015l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
