\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervening \highlight\uc2  Again \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Januar 1998\par 23:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have been swelled by the Bank of Israel's tight monetary policy, which has tamed inflation but has also created a large differential between interest rates in Israel and interest rates on major foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad. \par \par \uc2  That differential has encouraged customers to borrow in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and convert the money into shekels, thus strengthening the shekel. \par \par \uc2  In the first half of the year, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, buying more than $7 billion to weaken the shekel and keep it within its band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was staved off for half a year by the the June 18 widening of the shekel trading band and a 1.2-percentage-point cut in the discount rate to 12.7%. \par \par \uc2  Those two steps had the immediate effect of increasing the exchange rate risk in the minds of customers who had been borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and converting the loans into shekels. \par \par \uc2  But within weeks, the perception of an increased risk factor eased, and the shekel began inching back toward its ceiling. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key lending rate in September to 13.4% from 12.7%, with plans to keep it that high through January, the differential between Israel's interest rates and rates abroad made the shekel even more attractive, strengthening the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and making \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  just a matter of time. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday and Wednesday, the Bank of Israel was back in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying an estimated $220 million to $250 million. There is no foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading Thursday because of the New Year's holiday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say they don't know what will be required to keep near-daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from resuming. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-01-98 \par \par \uc2  2247GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1100095\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
