\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli bonds end steady in very active trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Dec 31 (Reuters) - Israeli inflation-linked bonds closed steady in very heavy trading on Wednesday as unlinked bonds closed higher on expectations of lower inflation in the coming months, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * Government bonds general: +0.01 pct to 112.44 \par \par \uc2  * CPI-linked government bonds: -0.03 pct to 111.33 \par \par \uc2  * Unlinked government bonds: +0.09 pct to 116.36 \par \par \uc2  * Dollar-linked government bonds: +0.10 pct to 113.54 \par \par \uc2  * Bank of Israel short-term Makam bills: +0.06 pct to 114.06 \par \par \uc2  Volume including Makams was a high 382 million shekels. \par \par \uc2  "Inflation-linked bonds closed steady today after the sharp declines yesterday. There was fairly big demand of 110 million shekels for unlinked bonds, and dollar bonds closed higher," said Assaf Yadid of Ilanot Batucha investment house. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the index of CPI-linked bonds closed 0.18 percent lower, which traders were at loss to explain. "It's still not clear what happened yesterday but today the market calmed down," Yadid said. \par \par \uc2  He said a combination of factors had probably caused Tuesday's falls, including investors' selling inflation-linked bonds to have liquidity for the beginning of the year, the bank of Israel's decision to keep interest rates unchanged another month; and lower-inflation estimates. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel said it was holding its key lending rate unchanged at 13.4 percent for January. The rate has been at that level since the end of August. \par \par \uc2  Economists have been lowering their inflation estimates for the coming 12 months, with some saying consumer prices will rise by just 6.6 percent next year. \par \par \uc2  "The low-inflation expectations are behind the demand for unlinked instruments," said Renan Mittelpunkt of the Financial Immunities consulting firm. But he said there could be renewed demand for inflation-linked bonds. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market increases the money supply, which could raise inflationary expectations and trigger renewed demand for inflation-linked bonds," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Wednesday for the second day running, buying an estimated $160 million to support the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We foresee that in the next quarter interest rates will fall gradually and yields of CPI-linked bonds will start falling again, despite the Treasury's annoucement that it will renew its bond issues in January," Yadid said. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury said on Wednesday it would issue in January 1.9 billion shekels worth of bonds after a one-month hiatus. It said it would issue one billion shekels worth of inflation-linked bonds for seven and 15 years and 900 million shekels worth of three-year unlinked bonds. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-linked bonds closed higher. The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5360 shekels against 3.5340 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Note: Makams are zero-coupon unlinked certificates with durations of three months to one year. The Bank of Israel issues Makams to absorb liquidity. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.53 shekels) ((Shoshanna Solomon , Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x233, telaviv.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcv00m4b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal258