\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Bank of Israel buys $160 mln in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Dec 31 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Wednesday for the second consecutive day, buying an estimated $160 million, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since June, buying about $70 million to support the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the basket's exchange rate reached the lower limit (the shekel's strong side) of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars again today to support the basket," said Guy Levi at Bank Leumi. He estimated that the bank purchased some $160 million. \par \par \uc2  "As long as interest rates remain high the shekel will stay at the current level and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to buy dollars," Levi said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel said on Monday that it was keeping its key lending rate unchanged at 13.4 percent for January. The rate has been at that level since the end of August. \par \par \uc2  Levi added that most of the activity came from the business sector, which was converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for end-of-the-year payments. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5360 shekels against 3.5340 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7861 against 3.7857 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7143 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.7282 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9728 shekels compared with 1.9718 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5320 shekels. \par \par \uc2  ((Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, +972 3 537-2211 x238, \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcv00m3e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
