\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Shekel Dn Vs Dlr, Up Vs Basket \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 15:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although the shekel traded lower against the dollar in late trading Tuesday, damped by the dollar's rise against the Deutsche mark, it strengthened against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that determines its place within the trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.5340 to the dollar, a weakening of 0.2% compared with Monday's close of 3.5270 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.5330 to 3.5370 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at 3.5330. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's strengthening against the basket was caused by a wave of dollar sales in the past two days. \par \par \uc2  Hundreds of millions of dollars were sold in the past two days in advance of Jan. 1 wage payments and the expiry of dollar-shekel options on the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange, said a dealer from Eurotrust Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Neil Corney, head of the spot desk at Bank Hapoalim, said he expected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  'will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the shekel moves back within the band.' \par \par \uc2  The band was widened in June after the Bank of Israel was forced to buy $7 billion from the beginning of the year to weaken the shekel and keep it within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Under the abandoned system, the shekel was allowed to fluctuate plus or minus 7% from a midpoint that depreciated 6% annually. \par \par \uc2  In addition to widening the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped the floor by 15%, though it continued to depreciate 6% annually. The ceiling was left unchanged, but is depreciating at a rate of 4% rather than 6% previously. \par \par \uc2  The change in the band's parameters, together with a simultaneous 1.2-percentage-point cut in the discount rate to 12.7%, caused the shekel to depreciate 5% within just a few days, halting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1420GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcu0a0du\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
