\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel: Public Sees Greater Exchange-Rate Risk \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 14:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The public has perceived a greater exchange-rate risk since the shekel trading band widened in June, the Bank of Israel said Tuesday, citing as evidence a doubling of demand for its shekel-dollar options. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the trading band June 18 after the shekel repeatedly strengthened to its strongest point within the band, forcing the Bank of Israel to buy more than $7 billion from the beginning of the year to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  One of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declared reasons for widening the band was to increase the exchange-rate risk, and the shekel depreciated some 5% immediately after the band was changed. \par \par \uc2  But although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading since June 17, the shekel has bounced back to hover just below its strongest point in the band. The discount rate is a high 13.4%, and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say customers are no longer as troubled by the higher exchange rate risk. \par \par \uc2  Demand for shekel-dollar options from July through November more than doubled in the first half of 1997, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a release. \par \par \uc2  From January through June average demand in each option auction was $9.9 million, compared with $21.1 million on average from July through November. \par \par \uc2  The rise in demand also led to higher prices of some 20% for three-month options and some 14% for six-month options. \par \par \uc2  The increased exchange-rate risk also was expressed in the slowdown in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The net total of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans rose $4.8 billion in the first half of 1997, compared with a rise of $700 million from July through November, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1307GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcu0a0bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
