\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Up Against Dollar in Late Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1997\par 15:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel traded higher against the dollar late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was less active than on Monday when the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market resumed full trading after a four-day strike, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.5340 to the dollar, a strengthening of 0.5% Monday's close of 3.5430 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.5310 to 3.5470 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at its strongest level for the day, at 3.5310. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dominated by dollar sales that strengthened the shekel, dealers said. One dealer attributed the sales to the last available day for paying wages in the business sector. \par \par \uc2  Israeli employers can pay salaries up to the ninth of every month, after which they are subject to paying interest to their workers. \par \par \uc2  In September and October the shekel weakened relatively against a dollar strengthened on world markets, but the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now approaching the strongest point in its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading once the shekel hits that ceiling, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading since it changed the shekel's trading band in mid-June. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prior to the change, the Bank of Israel bought 7 billion dollars in\par the first six months to weaken the shekel.\par   -By Michele Gershberg; 9722-537-6985; mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1421GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc909ge6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
