\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Rises As Dollar Weakens In Intl Markets \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1997\par 15:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel was trading higher against the shekel late Tuesday, fueled by the dollar's weakness against the Deutsche mark on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.5270 to the dollar, a strengthening of 0.2% compared with Monday's close of 3.5320 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of 3.5240 to 3.5330 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1330 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at 3.5270. \par \par \uc2  Yoav Shani, a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Hapoalim, said the dollar's general decline helped buoy the shekel. \par \par \uc2  Trading was light, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They noted the shekel was approaching the strongest point within its trading band, a warning signal on the Israeli market that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading again. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market since it\par changed the shekel's trading band on June 18. Until then, the Bank of\par Israel had bought some 7 billion dollars in 1997 to weaken the shekel.\par   -By Michele Gershberg; 972-2-537-6985; mgershberg@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1419GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc20987e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi