\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Borrowing Drops Since Band Change \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 1997\par 16:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Yet while these factors aren't generally influenced by Bank of Israel policy, continued borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, economists said. And Frenkel's reform at best only dampened that activity, some anaylsts said. \par \par \uc2  According to Shauli Katznelson, chief economist at Israel Discount Bank, 'if the discount rate would be cut between three to five percentage points, (the trend) could change direction.' \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been triggered by the conversion of 'hot money' customers brought into the economy in the first half of 1997 to take advantage of Israel's high interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The current 13.4% discount rate doesn't make borrowing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive for customers who benefit from the interest rate differentials when they convert the loans into shekels, Katznelson said. \par \par \uc2  Viskin countered that view, saying customers aren't borrowing as much in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they had done before the trading band was changed. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened because the dollar weakened on world markets, he argued. \par \par \uc2  And even if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Viskin says he doesn't expect it to start buying large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily as it had in the first half of the year. \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the trading band with an overly-strong shekel, the slowdown in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan-taking will minimize its purchase amounts, Viskin said. \par \par \uc2  Net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing dropped to $199 million in the third quarter of 1997 versus $4.2 billion in the first half of the year, the Bank of Israel said Sunday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1412GMT \par \par \uc2  1147 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtad07rq7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
