\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Strengthening May Force Bank Of Isael's Hand \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michele Gershberg \par \uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 1997\par 16:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel is inching closer to the strongest point in its trading band, and economists expect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market within weeks. \par \par \uc2  It would be the first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June 18, when the trading band was widened at the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's urging to halt its near-daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  The widening of the band had the immediate effect of devaluing the shekel by some 5% and pushing it as far as 4.2% below the ceiling, but the impact was short-lived. By midday Monday, the shekel was trading at 3.7600 versus a basket of major foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 0.39% below its ceiling. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the shekel at 3.7688 against the basket, 0.34% from the ceiling. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the shekel at 3.4950, down 0.4% from Thursday folowinf the long holiday weekend. \par \par \uc2  And the debate that arose immediately after the trading band was modified has resurged: Was the change a real step toward reforming the Israeli foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, or did it just give the Bank of Israel some breathing room? \par \par \uc2  'What we know is we are being dragged almost to the (ceiling),' of the trading band, said Gad Shifron, chief economist at Israel's No. 2 bank, Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  And once the shekel hits that point, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to defend the trading band, Shifron said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel could break through the ceiling of the band as early as next week, he predicted. \par \par \uc2  Ilan Viskin, head trader at Israel's largest bank, Bank Hapoalim, agreed the shekel was so close to its upper band that a random transaction on the Israeli market or a significant weakening of the dollar on world markets could push it above. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1408GMT \par \par \uc2  1147 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtad07rpd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
