\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel fixed 0.22 percent up on the dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Oct 9 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel resumed its advance on the dollar on Thursday, posting a new four-month high, following the decline of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark's rise helped boost the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the shekel, which has been trading close to the lower limit (or strong side) of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel rose against the dollar following the decline of the dollar against the mark," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the dollar, which was just above 1.7500 marks in dropped to 1.7399 after Germany's Bundesbank raised its key money market interest rate, the repo, to 3.30 percent from 3.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The shekel gained 0.22 percent rising to 3.4820 against the dollar, its highest level since mid-June when the twin announcements of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms and a sharp cut in interest rates caused the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drop sharply. \par \par \uc2  "Following the rise of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the basket recovered rising to 0.3 percent above the lower limit of the trading band. If the dollar continues to decline, the basket will rise and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not set a representative rate because of the Yom Kippur eve holiday. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4820 shekels against 3.4900 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7639 against 3.7593 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8771 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.8855 on Wednesday, and against the mark at 2.0066 shekels compared with 1.9839 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.4800 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x238 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta901gv2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
