\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel slightly lower against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Oct 8 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel on Wednesday weakened slightly against the dollar following the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains abroad, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was dull and the shekel traded in a narrow range throughout the day at about 3.49 shekels per dollar," said Guy Levi at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  He said the shekel's decline against the dollar followed the recovery of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the mark overseas. \par \par \uc2  "The basket remained flat at only 0.2 percent above the lower limit (the shekel's strong side) of the trading band. The trend is clear and the basket is expected to reach the lower edge," Levi said. "The question is when will it happen?" \par \par \uc2  "Activity is expected to remain low over the next few weeks until after the Jewish holidays. After that, the basket may reach the bottom," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Jewish holiday period ends on October 23. \par \par \uc2  If the basket reaches the limit the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the shekel from strengthening beyond the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed out of the market since mid-June, when the twin announcements of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms and a 1.2 percentage point cut in interest rates set off a sharp depreciation of the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Since early July, however, the shekel has been gradually regaining on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.4900 shekels against 3.4850 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7593 against 3.7597 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8855 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.8627 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9839 shekels compared with 1.9942 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.4900 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x238 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta801enr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
