\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Shekel Up 0.2% Against Dlr In Sept. Vs. Aug. \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1997\par 17:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The shekel strengthened 0.2% against the dollar in September compared to the previous month, the Central Bureau of Statistics reported Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's appreciation against the dollar has slowed since July this year. In July, the shekel strengthened 1.3% compared to the dollar, and rose 0.7% in August. \par \par \uc2  The increases followed a sharp 5.7% depreciation of the shekel in June, occurring mainly after the Bank of Israel changed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading formula. \par \par \uc2  The rationale was to gradually depreciate the shekel without Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Prior to the reform, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $7 billion since January to weaken the shekel and force it back within its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Allen Langner, a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Eurotrust Ltd., said the shekel is appreciating slower as it approaches the ceiling of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  'The market stops itself' just before closing the gap, he said, but predicted it was just a matter of time before the limit was reached. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading again if the shekel strengthens beyond its ceiling. \par \par \uc2  The bureau noted it compared the exchange rates from Aug. 31 and Sept. 29 in advance of the Jewish New Year holiday this week. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-09-97 \par \par 