\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel rises against basket, down vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 2 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel rose to its highest level since June against the basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesd dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The market has been very quiet during the last few days. Today the shekel traded in a narrow range of 3.513-3.519 shekels per dollar," said Gideon Sadeh at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  "The most interesting thing was that the basket fell to only 0.4 percent above the lower limit (or strong side) of the trading band, which is the lowest level since June," he said. \par \par \uc2  Sadeh added that if the strengthening of the shekel against the basket continued the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since June, when \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform and a 1.2 percentage point cut in interest rates set off a sharp depreciation of the shekel. \par \par \uc2  Sadeh said the shekel weakened on Tuesday against the dollar following the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise abroad. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5160 shekels compared with 3.5120 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7508 against 3.7534 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against at 2.8901 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9040 on Monday, and against the mark at 1.9299 shekels compared with 1.9347 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5150 shekels. \par \par \uc2  -- Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x238 DMG TCC \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt9200fs9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
