\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel ends higher against the dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 26 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel was fixed sharply higher against the dollar on Tuesday but dealers said the representative rate did not reflect the market trend, which was much more muted. \par \par \uc2  "The market did not react to the (interest) rate hike. The most dominant factor today was the expiry of the Maof dollar options for August," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Bank of Israel announced that the base rate would rise 0.7 percentage point for September to an annualised 13.4 percent. The increase was above market expectations and marked the first rise in rates since July 1996. \par \par \uc2  The Mizrahi dealer said the dollar was traded downwards against the shekel in response to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp decline against the mark overseas. The shekel also declined sharply against the mark. \par \par \uc2  But options speculators offset the mark's impact by supporting the dollar, said Olivier Hakoune of Union Bank. "The options speculators prevented the shekel from rising further against the dollar after the rate announcement," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Mizrahi dealer said the interest rate hike had not prompted a renewed wave of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked borrowing. "On the contrary, investors are trying to close foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans," she said. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced last week foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms is preventing investors from taking \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans. They are afraid of a speculative attack on the shekel," she added. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel and Treasury unveiled a package of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms last Thursday to bring the shekel a step towards becoming a fully convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a year. \par \par \uc2  Hakoune said he expected the shekel to continue rising in the next several days. "The basket will fall to the lower limit (or strong side) of its trading band and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June, before it slashed interest rates by 1.2 percentage points and set off a sharp depreciation of the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5150 shekels compared with 3.5310 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7721 against 3.7724 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9806 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9860 on Monday, and against the mark at 1.9565 shekels compared with 1.9364 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5250 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x238 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8q00n24\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
