\par\par \b \uc2  Israel shekel gains on dollar ahead of CPI release. \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 14 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel strengthened against the dollar on Thursday in advance of the release on Friday of what is expected to be a high July consumer price index (CPI), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel weakened slightly against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the mark as the dollar fell abroad. \par \par \uc2  "In the morning the basket was a lot higher. Then we saw conversions of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels and the basket began to drop as the dollar/shekel rate fell," a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank said. \par \par \uc2  "If July's CPI is above one percent the Bank of Israel will likely raise interest rates," she said. \par \par \uc2  The business sector also converted foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in advance of value-added tax payments due on August 15. \par \par \uc2  The basket rate is now less than one percent above the lower limit, or strong side, of its trading band against the shekel. \par \par \uc2  If the basket reaches the limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from strengthening beyond its band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June, when it slashed interest rates by 1.2 percentage points following a government decision to widen the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5290 shekels compared with 3.5340 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7634 against 3.7628 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0284 shekels per 100 yen, compared with 3.0396 on Wednesday, and against the mark at 1.9222 shekels compared with 1.9152. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5277 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Tova Cohen, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x238 TCC DER \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e01982\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
