\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel sharply higher vs dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 7 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel rose sharply against the dollar and basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and dealers said that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  once more in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The session opened with low activity and the market was quiet," said Gideon Sadeh at Bank Leumi. "By midday the business sector started converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels and the shekel rose sharply." \par \par \uc2  Sadeh said there was no evident reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversions of the companies. \par \par \uc2  He added that the shekel was traded at only 0.5 percent below the higher edge of its trading band. "The market expects that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to start buying dollars soon, maybe even next week, to prevent the shekel from strengthening beyond its band," Sadeh said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in mid-June, after it slashed interest rates by 1.2 percentage points following a government decision to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band and lower its crawling slope. \par \par \uc2  Sadeh added that in the near term the shekel is expected to move in a range of 3.52 to 3.535 shekels per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.5290 shekels compared with 3.5410 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.7414 against 3.7506 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9712 shekels per 100 yen compared with 2.9683 on Wednesday, and against the mark at 1.8764 shekels compared with 1.8762 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon, the dollar was trading at 3.5300 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8701hgu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
